      "description": "The (Vowel + Consonant)உயிர்மெய் எழுத்துக்கள் are compound letters in Tamil formed by combining a consonant (மெய்) with a vowel (உயிர்). For example, the consonant ன்(n) combines with vowels to form ன, னா, னி, னீ, னு, னூ, னெ, னே, னை, னொ, னோ, and னௌ."
